@startuml code-device-onboarding
title Sequence diagram (C4, level 4) - self-service device onboarding\nDevice Management Service

actor Homeowner
participant "Web/Mobile Client" as Client
participant "API Gateway\n(YARP)" as Gateway
participant "API\n(REST controllers)" as Api
participant "OnboardingHandler" as Onboarding
participant "Device Gateway\n(protocol adapter)" as DeviceGw
participant "Device State Manager" as StateMgr
participant "IDeviceRepository" as Repo
database "Device Management DB" as Db
participant "Physical/Partner Device" as Device

Homeowner -> Client: Enter pairing code for new device
Client -> Gateway: POST /devices/onboard {deviceType, pairingCode}
Gateway -> Api: Routes request
Api -> Onboarding: StartOnboarding(homeId, deviceType, pairingCode)

Onboarding -> DeviceGw: NegotiateProtocol(pairingCode, deviceType)
DeviceGw -> Device: Discovery/handshake over standard protocol
Device --> DeviceGw: deviceId, capabilities, protocolConfig

alt device unreachable or pairing code invalid
    DeviceGw --> Onboarding: PairingFailed(reason)
    Onboarding --> Api: OnboardingResult.Failure(reason)
    Api --> Gateway: 400 Bad Request
    Gateway --> Client: Show pairing error
else pairing succeeds
    DeviceGw --> Onboarding: PairingResult(deviceId, capabilities, protocolConfig)

    Onboarding -> StateMgr: RegisterDevice(homeId, deviceId, deviceType, protocolConfig)
    StateMgr -> StateMgr: new Device(homeId, deviceId, deviceType, protocolConfig)
    StateMgr -> Repo: Save(device)
    Repo -> Db: INSERT INTO devices (...)
    Db --> Repo: OK
    Repo --> StateMgr: device
    StateMgr --> Onboarding: device

    Onboarding --> Api: OnboardingResult.Success(device)
    Api --> Gateway: 201 Created {device}
    Gateway --> Client: Show "device connected"
    Client --> Homeowner: Device now visible in the app
end

@enduml
